          "filename": "John Knox House, Edinburgh - geograph.org.uk - 506114.jpg",
          "caption": "John Knox House, Edinburgh Situated on the Royal Mile, the rear of this old house was built not long after 1450 and the frontage added around 1472. Additions and modifications have been made ever since. Although named John Knox House, after the great reformer of the church in Scotland, there is no record of him ever staying in it.\nThe house is now a museum, based on John Knox, and has become a popular tourist attraction.",
          "alt": "John Knox House, Edinburgh Situated on the Royal Mile, the rear of this old house was built not long after 1450 and the frontage added around 1472. Additions and modifications have been made ever since. Although named John Knox House, after the great reformer of the church in Scotland, there is no record of him ever staying in it.\nThe house is now a museum, based on John Knox, and has become a popular tourist attraction.",
